<txp:hide>
  The header for most pages. Switches and knobs: see o_header and scss/4-organisms/_o_header.scss.
  Or open the debug toolbar's Header panel, try things, and Copy the tag back in here.

  o_header--over-hero: over the image on pages with a .u_hero (see pages/default.txp,
  the sticky article's class), a normal header everywhere else. No TXP logic needed.

  Overlay menu on phones, inline from medium up (replaces the old two-header hamburger set-up):
  <txp::o_header class="o_header--split o_header--sticky" style="--o-header-max: 1720px" menu="overlay" inline="medium" />
</txp:hide>
<txp::o_header
  class='
    o_header--split
    o_header--sticky
    o_header--forehead
  '
  style="--o-header-max: var(--width-large)"
  menu="overlay"
  inline="medium"
/>